.Sh HISTORY
Written for
.Xr kldload 7 ,
which ships it preinstalled, and published separately so it can be used and
updated without adopting a substrate.
Nothing in the harness knows about kldload: a stock Debian host with
.Sy zfsutils-linux
and
.Sy libvirt-daemon-system
runs it.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An kldload Aq Mt anthony@kldload.com
.Sh CAVEATS
One VM runs at a time.
Memory is sized from what the host has free on the assumption that nothing
else is competing, so a run on a busy hypervisor will size small or collide.
.Pp
The first golden build needs a network to fetch cloud images.
Afterwards the images are cached and rebuilds are local.
.Pp
Results live at
.Pa /root/kzfs-test
and the cloud image cache at
.Pa /var/lib/libvirt/isos ;
both paths are currently fixed.
.Pp
Root is required.
The harness drives libvirt, creates zvols and writes under
.Pa /root .
.Pp
A golden is a point in time.
The distribution it came from keeps moving, so a golden built months ago
tests the kernel and ZFS of months ago.
That is sometimes exactly what you want and sometimes not what you meant.
.Cm kzfs-test status
prints the kernel and ZFS each golden actually carries; read it before
trusting an old matrix.
